counttr -- a mental arithmetic trainer
======================================

counttr is a mathematics count trainer for the terminal, written in
Lua.  It asks you questions in the chosen mode (squares, addition,
multiplication, subtraction, floor division, roots, powers or modulo)
and checks your answers.

Screenshot: example.jpeg

Requirements
------------

Lua 5.4 or later and LuaRocks 3.9.2 or later, because the mfr and
argparse rocks are required.  All of these are installed automatically
if you use the Arch Linux package (see below).

Building and installing
-----------------------

On Arch Linux, clone this repository and build and install the package
from the project's directory:

    makepkg -sri

Elsewhere, "make all" installs the two rocks into your home directory
with "luarocks install --local" and copies main.lua to counttr.

Using it
--------

Once installed, run it as

    counttr OPTIONS MODE

and otherwise as

    lua main.lua OPTIONS MODE

Help is available with the --help option:

    Arguments:
       {squares,add,multiply,substract,floor_division,root,power,modulo}
                             training mode
    Options:
       -h, --help            Show this help message and exit.
       --completion {bash,zsh,fish}
                             Output a shell completion script for the
                             specified shell.
       --repeat <repeat>     number of repetitions
       --from <from>         smaller range border
       --to <to>             larger range border
       --power <power>       power for power action or root
       -n, --no-colors       disable use of colorful output with ascii
                             control sequences
       -c, --colors          (forced) use of colorful output with ascii
                             control sequences. by default, colors are
                             enabled if NO_COLORS environment variable
                             is not set and terminal emulator supports
                             colors.

Reporting bugs
--------------

counttr is open for ideas, bug reports and contributions:
https://github.com/mb6ockatf/counttr/issues.

